  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-ui-draggable (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package executes a bundled dropper (_runtime.js) that fingerprints the OS/arch and downloads a platform-specific second-stage binary over HTTPS from three Cloudflare Workers hosts (oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. If the HTTPS download fails, it reconstructs the payload from base64 chunks retrieved via DNS TXT queries against c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and sdk/ext/pkg/net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru per platform). The downloaded binary is written to the temp dir (as.cache_\u003chex\u003e on Unix, dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows), chmod 755, and launched detached via /bin/sh or cmd.exe so it outlives the parent. A rate-limit stamp file (.analytics_state / analytics_state) suppresses repeat execution.",
